<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco cuts bunker prices.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco cuts bunker prices.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has cut the prices of its A-888 bunker diesel from Ras Tanura and Dammam to $211 a tonne from $236 effective January 30, the company said.</p>
<p>A-888 bunker diesel from the Red Sea was cut to $216 a tonne from $240.</p>
<p>From the Gulf, A-960 bunker fuel oil is dropped to $105 a tonne ($16.12 a barrel) from $120 a tonne. From Jeddah and Yanbu A-960 bunker fuel oil is also lower at $105 a tonne ($16.12 a barrel) from $124 a tonne.</p>
</text>
